@startuml network-flows-table
' ============================================================================
' LinID Identity Manager — Network Flows (Table View)
' Companion to network-flows.puml: keep both files in sync.
' Ports are those of the e2e environment (docker/e2e/docker-compose.yml).
' ============================================================================

skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam defaultFontName "DejaVu Sans"
skinparam noteFontSize 8

title LinID Identity Manager — Network Flows (Table, e2e environment)

note
  **Current flows (F1–F18)**
  |= ID |= Source |= Destination |= Port |= Protocol |= Direction |= Authentication |= Encryption |= Scope |
  | F1  | Browser    | UI server        | 9000 -> 443  | HTTPS      | Inbound  | Session cookie         | TLS        | External |
  | F2  | Browser    | UI server (/auth/ -> LemonLDAP portal) | 9000 -> 443 | HTTPS | Inbound | Username / password | TLS | External |
  | F3  | Admin      | Apache Superset  | 8088 -> 8443 | HTTPS      | Inbound  | Username / password    | TLS        | External |
  | F4  | Browser    | Apache Superset  | 8088 -> 8443 | HTTPS      | Inbound  | Guest token            | TLS        | External |
  | F5  | Admin      | LinID API        | 8443         | HTTPS      | Inbound  | JWT                    | TLS        | External |
  | F6  | UI server  | LinID API        | 8443         | HTTPS/REST | Outbound | JWT bearer             | TLS        | Internal |
  | F7  | UI server  | LemonLDAP::NG    | 80           | HTTP       | Outbound | Portal session / JWT bearer | None  | Internal |
  | F8  | UI server  | LemonLDAP::NG    | 80           | HTTP       | Outbound | Client id / secret     | None       | Internal |
  | F9  | UI server  | LinPulsar        | 80           | HTTP       | Outbound | None                   | None       | Internal |
  | F10 | LinID API  | PostgreSQL       | 5432         | JDBC       | Outbound | DB user / password     | None       | Internal |
  | F11 | LinID API  | OPA              | 8181         | REST/HTTP  | Outbound | None                   | None       | Internal |
  | F12 | LinID API  | UI server        | 443          | HTTPS      | Outbound | None (public JWKS)     | TLS        | Internal |
  | F13 | LinID API  | Apache Superset  | 8443         | REST/HTTPS | Outbound | Service account        | TLS        | Internal |
  | F14 | LinID API  | LinID Sync API   | 8443         | REST/HTTPS | Outbound | Client certificate     | Mutual TLS | Internal |
  | F15 | Sync API   | PostgreSQL       | 5432         | JDBC       | Outbound | DB user / password     | None       | Internal |
  | F16 | Sync API   | OPA              | 8181         | REST/HTTP  | Outbound | None                   | None       | Internal |
  | F17 | LemonLDAP  | PostgreSQL       | 5432         | DBI/Pg     | Outbound | DB user / password     | None       | Internal |
  | F18 | Superset   | PostgreSQL       | 5432         | SQLAlchemy | Outbound | DB user / password     | None       | Internal |
  ~~~~~~
  **Future flows (F19–F21): target architecture, not yet implemented**
  |= ID |= Source |= Destination |= Port |= Protocol |= Direction |= Authentication |= Encryption |= Scope |
  | F19 | Sync API   | External Referential | N/A      | REST/HTTPS | Outbound | Service account        | TLS         | External |
  | F20 | Sync API   | LDAP Directory   | 389 / 636    | LDAP       | Outbound | Service account        | TLS (LDAPS) | Internal |
  | F21 | LemonLDAP  | LDAP Directory   | 389 / 636    | LDAP       | Outbound | Service account        | TLS (LDAPS) | Internal |
  ~~~~~~
  **Notes**
  • Trust assumption: the plain-text internal flows (F7–F11, F15–F18) rely on the Docker network being private.
  • F1/F2: the browser only reaches the UI server. LemonLDAP::NG and LinPulsar have no host port; the UI server
    proxies /auth/, /static/, /index.psgi to LemonLDAP (F7) and /lin-pulsar/ to LinPulsar (F9).
  • F4: Superset dashboards are embedded by the LinPulsar SupersetWidgetCard, with guest tokens issued by the API (F13).
    Superset is optional: it is not deployed in the demo environment.
  • F7: the userinfo endpoint (/auth/me) is called with the access token of the session (JWT bearer).
  • F8: OIDC discovery runs once at startup on the internal URL of LemonLDAP (issuer http://auth); code exchange and
    token refresh are server to server, the tokens never reach the browser.
  • F12: the API fetches the JWKS through the UI server (AUTH_JWK_SET_URI=https://ui/auth/oauth2/jwks) with a
    truststore containing the UI server certificate; the UI server then proxies the request to LemonLDAP (F7).
  • F14: sync-api requires a client certificate (client-auth: need) and only accepts linid-api.
  • F15: sync-api reads accounts and writes computed_rights in the linid DB, and stores its Spring Batch metadata in
    the sync_api DB.
  • F18: Superset uses two databases (superset metadata + datalake) on the same instance, with different credentials.
  • e2e only: OPA (8181), Sync API (8444 -> 8443) and PostgreSQL (5432) are also published on the host for the tests.
    In the demo environment, the API (8443), OPA (8181) and PostgreSQL are published. Only the UI server (and
    Superset if used) should be exposed in production.
  • F20/F21: LDAP port 389 (STARTTLS) or 636 (LDAPS), to be confirmed at implementation time.
end note

@enduml
